API-01: refuse forcing values set before swmm_start instead of discarding them

swmm_setValue and swmm_setValueExpanded accepted a gage rainfall, a node
lateral inflow, a link setting and a subcatchment's API rainfall, snowfall
and PET before swmm_start and returned 0, but swmm_start resets all of them
(gage_initState, node_initState, link_initState, subcatch_initState), so the
run never used the value. Return ERR_API_NOT_STARTED for these properties
until the simulation has started, as 6.0.0 does (SWMM_ERR_LIFECYCLE). A value
set after swmm_start and before the first swmm_step is used from the first
step, exactly as before. The node and link pollutant mass fluxes have the
same problem but are left to CRASH-13, which fixes their pre-start branch.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-01_swmm530.patch

